Subject: [PATCH v10 00/10] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build the list's mail hub
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:41:38 +0000

This builds the hub that "[PATCH v2] jails/instances/lab-mail: Spec
the list's mail hub" [1] describes, on b/dev. It turns the relay jail
into the list's home in steps, one service at a time. Each step
leaves a jail that works and does what its README.org says.

How mail moves, end to end, once the series is applied:

  client --SMTP--> OpenSMTPD --LMTP--> Dovecot --> INBOX
  Dovecot <--IMAP--> mbsync <--IMAPS--> Fastmail
    (INBOX, Next, Later, and Archive only)

New mail lands in INBOX, whether it is posted to lab-mail or arrives
at Fastmail. lab-mail syncs exactly four folders with Fastmail: INBOX,
Next, Later, and Archive. Any other folder Pat makes on Fastmail
stays there, and reaches neither lab-mail nor any notmuch. There is no
lists folder, no Sieve, and no Fastmail rule. Dovecot is the only
program that writes the maildir. Every reader may read every folder,
and only Pat and mbsync may change anything.

- Patch 1 corrects the spec on what Dovecot does to a reader's write.
  A STORE or EXPUNGE answers OK and changes nothing. Only append,
  copy, and move are refused.
- Patch 2 narrows the spec's header check to what OpenSMTPD does on
  its own.
- Patch 3 changes the spec to keep the list in INBOX of the list's
  own account, and to sync INBOX and Archive and no other folder. The
  Fastmail rule, the lists folder, and the moderation queue go.
- Patch 4 makes Dovecot the only writer of the list. mbsync fetches
  Fastmail's INBOX one way into Dovecot's INBOX over IMAP, as the
  login mbsync. This is the one step that needs the maildir and
  mbsync's state emptied first.
- Patch 5 turns the fetch into a two-way sync of INBOX and Archive.
- Patch 6 adds Pat's login, so he can archive and delete on lab-mail.
- Patch 7 swaps smtprelay for OpenSMTPD, which hands posts to Dovecot
  over LMTP, into INBOX. smtprelay, jq, and the mailcred group go
  with it.
- Patch 8 documents the one-time import of the jj maildir into INBOX.
- Patch 9 adds lab@lists.p7x.dev and freebsd-ports@lists.p7x.dev to
  the addresses OpenSMTPD delivers to the list.
- Patch 10 syncs Next and Later beside INBOX and Archive, and specs
  the client side: the folder is a message's only state, clients
  derive their tags from it, and Pat's notmuch syncs flags.

Before deploying: delete the Fastmail rule that files list mail into
lists, and create Next and Later on Fastmail. mbsync creates no
folder. Mail still in lists on Fastmail stays there, outside the
list, until you move it to INBOX or Archive.

For every step I checked that each libexec script passes sh -n, and
mbsync 1.5.1 parses the mbsyncrc of patches 4, 5, and 10. Dovecot,
smtpd, and the jail build are not installed here, so no step was run
on a jail.

Changes in v10:
- lab-mail syncs only INBOX, Next, Later, and Archive (Patterns with
  Create None), not every folder, so folders made on Fastmail for
  anything else stay out of notmuch (Pat). mbsync loses the ACL's
  create right again.
- The lists folder never appears. Patch 3 is new and moves the list
  into INBOX in the spec first. Patches 4 to 9 then build on INBOX,
  so v9's "Deliver posts to INBOX and sync it" is folded into them
  and dropped.
- Patch 10 no longer names quarantine, which is not one of the
  synced folders. It now also adds Next and Later to lab-mail's
  sync and Dovecot, and its subject is "Sync the Next and Later
  folders".
- Patches 1 and 2 are unchanged.
